LRC FORMAL CERTIFICATE TRILEMMA
For a speed set V at denominator n, a no-lonely open cover must pass:
  1. denominator sieve completeness (THM-366/369),
  2. nonempty terminal endpoint protection core (THM-357/359),
  3. a cyclic owner-pressure graph if core protection is pressure-realized (THM-379/380).

Therefore a proof search can stop on any of these certificates:
  missing small denominator -> rational lonely witness;
  empty endpoint core       -> no all-protected open cover;
  pressure DAG + realized core incidences -> no counterexample core.

The remaining disproof-shaped object is narrow:
  sieve-complete + nonempty endpoint core + nontrivial labelled pressure SCC.
